        "thinking": "I'm weighing whether to pick leaving or staying in Le Guin's story. Leaving looks like the only fully moral choice to me, since staying means knowingly accepting the child's suffering as the price of everyone else's comfort, so I'm leaning toward answering A.\n\nI'm keeping it short and acknowledging the discomfort that comes with choosing to leave.\n\n",
        "type": "thinking"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "A) Leave forever.\n\nI couldn't knowingly keep my comfort at a child's expense, even though leaving changes nothing for the child. Staying would mean accepting that my happiness rests on that suffering, and I think that would corrupt the life I was trying to protect.",
